1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:01:00,320
= kisskh.asia =

2
00:00:00,259 --> 00:00:01,259
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:01,259 --> 00:00:02,259
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:02,259 --> 00:00:03,437
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:04,426 --> 00:00:07,855
[Episode 8]

6
00:00:07,855 --> 00:00:10,151
I told you I'm all better.

7
00:00:10,151 --> 00:00:13,587
I was cooped up in a hospital for months.
I just needed to get out.

8
00:00:13,587 --> 00:00:17,919
The doctor said you shouldn't
push yourself for a while.

9
00:00:17,919 --> 00:00:20,735
You've only been out for a few days.
Why go somewhere that rough?

10
00:00:20,735 --> 00:00:22,831
Come on, if it were that rough,
I wouldn't have made it here.

11
00:00:22,831 --> 00:00:26,692
The roads are much better these days.
They go all the way up to the lodge...

12
00:00:28,791 --> 00:00:31,667
Oh... Mom, I'm in the mountains,
so the signal is bad.

13
00:00:31,667 --> 00:00:32,830
I'll eat well, get plenty of rest,

14
00:00:32,830 --> 00:00:34,891
and head back in a week,
so don't worry too much.

15
00:00:34,891 --> 00:00:36,591
I'm hanging up now.

16
00:00:43,843 --> 00:00:45,727
Hello! How have you been?

17
00:00:45,727 --> 00:00:47,087
Oh, welcome.

18
00:00:47,087 --> 00:00:48,127
Have you been well?

19
00:00:48,127 --> 00:00:50,475
Oh, careful, it's slippery.

20
00:00:50,475 --> 00:00:51,763
Why are you out in this cold?

21
00:00:51,763 --> 00:00:53,159
You've been well, right?

22
00:00:53,159 --> 00:00:57,523
You usually come toward the end of summer.
What brings you here in the winter?

23
00:00:57,523 --> 00:01:00,931
I had some things to take care of,
so it turned out this way.

24
00:01:00,931 --> 00:01:04,591
The road was rough, so you had
a hard time getting up here, huh?

25
00:01:04,591 --> 00:01:06,495
Yeah, it took a little longer than usual.

26
00:01:06,495 --> 00:01:09,015
Oh, you're lucky the weather's good today.

27
00:01:09,015 --> 00:01:10,792
Once it snows, you can't even get up here.

28
00:01:10,792 --> 00:01:15,726
In the winter, you can only come and go
if the mountain allows it.

29
00:01:15,726 --> 00:01:19,591
You must be tired.
Go on up, unpack, and get some rest.

30
00:01:19,591 --> 00:01:21,139
Okay, it's the same room
I always stay in, right?

31
00:01:21,139 --> 00:01:22,547
No, the room next door.

32
00:01:22,547 --> 00:01:24,091
That one's occupied.

33
00:01:24,091 --> 00:01:25,791
Occupied?

34
00:01:27,607 --> 00:01:30,143
A young woman came a few days ago.

35
00:01:30,143 --> 00:01:32,583
She seems to have no energy.
She just sleeps all day.

36
00:01:32,583 --> 00:01:34,395
She's always collapsing wherever she is.

37
00:01:34,395 --> 00:01:37,192
Oh, I'm worried sick about her.

38
00:02:25,155 --> 00:02:26,855
Excuse...

39
00:02:35,495 --> 00:02:37,559
Doesn't she remember me?

40
00:02:44,059 --> 00:02:45,059
Good morning!

41
00:02:45,059 --> 00:02:47,047
- Oh, welcome!
- Welcome.

42
00:02:47,047 --> 00:02:49,126
Have a seat.

43
00:02:49,126 --> 00:02:50,859
Alright.

44
00:02:54,779 --> 00:02:56,067
Oh, the woman in the next room?

45
00:02:56,067 --> 00:02:59,095
That young lady doesn't
usually eat breakfast.

46
00:02:59,095 --> 00:03:01,087
It would be a relief
if she just skipped breakfast.

47
00:03:01,087 --> 00:03:04,099
She skips lunch and dinner even more often.

48
00:03:04,099 --> 00:03:07,531
Even when she sits down for a meal,
she barely eats a few bites.

49
00:03:07,531 --> 00:03:09,163
How long is she staying?

50
00:03:09,163 --> 00:03:13,967
She paid a month's room
and meal fees up front, but who knows.

51
00:03:13,967 --> 00:03:18,599
There isn't much to do around here.
She might get bored and leave early.

52
00:03:18,599 --> 00:03:21,911
How long are you staying this time?

53
00:03:21,911 --> 00:03:24,026
Well, I was thinking about a week...

54
00:03:26,071 --> 00:03:30,192
I'm thinking of staying
until I get a little bored of it this time.

55
00:03:34,451 --> 00:03:37,392
Oh, come over here and have a bite with us.

56
00:03:39,819 --> 00:03:41,211
Oh, jeez.

57
00:03:41,211 --> 00:03:42,859
Come on, eat.

58
00:03:42,859 --> 00:03:44,459
Okay.

59
00:03:44,459 --> 00:03:49,111
She's so quiet. Looks like
she's heading back into the mountains.

60
00:03:49,111 --> 00:03:51,395
I don't know where she gets
the energy when she barely eats.

61
00:03:51,395 --> 00:03:54,992
Still, it's better than
sleeping in her room all day.

62
00:03:58,967 --> 00:04:01,423
Don't we have too little meat?

63
00:04:01,423 --> 00:04:03,495
Should we grill some meat for dinner?

64
00:04:03,495 --> 00:04:06,159
Yeah, sounds good.

65
00:04:36,583 --> 00:04:38,283
Huh?

66
00:04:41,119 --> 00:04:42,239
Oh...

67
00:04:42,239 --> 00:04:45,035
Wow, you walk incredibly fast.

68
00:04:45,035 --> 00:04:48,535
I thought you were using
some kind of magic shortcut.

69
00:04:48,535 --> 00:04:51,026
I guess you like hiking, huh?

70
00:04:52,807 --> 00:04:54,592
I'm not usually weak in the legs.

71
00:04:54,592 --> 00:04:57,819
It's just that the terrain
around here is pretty rough.

72
00:04:57,819 --> 00:04:59,979
And I had a pretty serious injury recently,

73
00:04:59,979 --> 00:05:02,192
so I spent quite a while in the hospital.

74
00:05:02,192 --> 00:05:05,123
Do you happen to know
Gyeongsan Hospital in Gyeongsan-dong?

75
00:05:05,123 --> 00:05:07,183
Darn it! Ah!

76
00:05:12,451 --> 00:05:16,492
We're having a barbecue tonight.
You have to join us!

77
00:05:18,823 --> 00:05:21,359
Still so aloof.

78
00:05:32,171 --> 00:05:34,759
I see you prefer protein.

79
00:05:35,811 --> 00:05:37,959
Honey, hurry up and grill the meat.
Please grill all of it.

80
00:05:37,959 --> 00:05:42,051
Yeah, we'll have to stock up on meat
next time we go grocery shopping.

81
00:05:49,339 --> 00:05:53,839
By the way, when are you going
to bring your girlfriend?

82
00:05:53,839 --> 00:05:56,431
Don't you get tired of always coming alone?

83
00:05:56,431 --> 00:06:01,392
I haven't met my perfect match
like you two yet.

84
00:06:02,626 --> 00:06:04,399
Honey, the fire's getting low.

85
00:06:04,399 --> 00:06:08,203
I need to get some dry firewood
from the shed.

86
00:06:08,203 --> 00:06:10,171
I'll get it.

87
00:06:10,171 --> 00:06:11,992
Okay, sure.

88
00:06:22,995 --> 00:06:24,992
Give it to me. I'll carry it.

89
00:06:30,059 --> 00:06:32,847
Don't you remember me?
We've met before. Twice.

90
00:06:32,847 --> 00:06:34,683
- Yes, I remember.
- Right?

91
00:06:34,683 --> 00:06:36,559
I knew you'd remember.

92
00:06:36,559 --> 00:06:38,859
Wow, meeting for a third time
all the way out here!

93
00:06:38,859 --> 00:06:41,926
Isn't this an incredible coincidence?

94
00:06:41,926 --> 00:06:44,171
How could something like this happen?

95
00:06:44,171 --> 00:06:46,459
This is such a remote place,
and hardly anyone knows about it.

96
00:06:46,459 --> 00:06:49,355
At this point, I'd say we have
a pretty unusual connection.

97
00:06:49,355 --> 00:06:51,055
Excuse me.

98
00:06:52,763 --> 00:06:53,763
Yes?

99
00:06:53,763 --> 00:06:56,771
I came here
because I don't want to do anything.

100
00:06:56,771 --> 00:06:59,292
- Pardon?
- I just want some peace and quiet.

101
00:07:11,507 --> 00:07:13,492
I'm the one staying in the room next door.

102
00:07:18,635 --> 00:07:22,063
The owners went down
the mountain early this morning.

103
00:07:22,063 --> 00:07:24,192
It's their monthly grocery shopping day.

104
00:07:24,192 --> 00:07:26,463
They asked me to make sure you eat.

105
00:07:26,463 --> 00:07:29,126
But you hadn't come down by lunchtime.

106
00:07:30,111 --> 00:07:32,863
I won't ask you to do anything or bother you.

107
00:07:32,863 --> 00:07:34,692
So let's just eat.

108
00:07:35,311 --> 00:07:38,992
Come down whenever you feel like it.
I'll be waiting.

109
00:09:23,323 --> 00:09:25,026
Excuse me!

110
00:09:26,431 --> 00:09:29,326
I think you should come outside for a moment.

111
00:09:30,339 --> 00:09:32,039
Excuse me?

112
00:09:36,683 --> 00:09:40,126
I just got a call from the owner.

113
00:09:40,126 --> 00:09:43,367
All roads leading into the mountain
have been closed since yesterday afternoon.

114
00:09:43,367 --> 00:09:46,435
And they've just imposed
an indefinite ban on entry.

115
00:09:46,435 --> 00:09:48,592
Looks like we're stranded.

116
00:10:19,675 --> 00:10:21,355
Where have you been?

117
00:10:21,355 --> 00:10:23,126
Put some clothes on and come out.

118
00:10:44,571 --> 00:10:47,826
So this is where they store
all the food supplies.

119
00:10:50,835 --> 00:10:52,467
But how did you find...

120
00:10:52,467 --> 00:10:54,292
I found out when I came to get some firewood.

121
00:10:54,292 --> 00:10:59,087
Let's take the things that'll spoil quickly
or can't be eaten once frozen.

122
00:10:59,087 --> 00:11:00,792
Oh, okay.

123
00:11:02,279 --> 00:11:04,287
There isn't much left here either.

124
00:11:04,287 --> 00:11:05,434
Still, if we ration it,

125
00:11:05,434 --> 00:11:07,343
the two of us should
be able to make it for about a week, right?

126
00:11:07,343 --> 00:11:09,415
The roads will be open by then, right?

127
00:11:09,415 --> 00:11:11,359
It could take longer.

128
00:11:18,855 --> 00:11:20,575
Oh, oh!

129
00:11:20,575 --> 00:11:21,711
It's okay.

130
00:11:21,711 --> 00:11:24,859
Oh, this is for hunting.
That startled you, right?

131
00:11:24,859 --> 00:11:29,047
Lodges this deep in the mountains
usually keep one of these around.

132
00:11:29,047 --> 00:11:30,892
Because of wild animals.

133
00:11:35,131 --> 00:11:37,459
Oh, don't touch that carelessly...

134
00:11:38,871 --> 00:11:40,571
It's dangerous.

135
00:11:56,867 --> 00:11:58,951
Wait, those are bullets?

136
00:11:58,951 --> 00:12:00,894
That's...

137
00:12:00,894 --> 00:12:03,292
Why are you taking those...

138
00:12:06,815 --> 00:12:09,826
Huh? Why are you... Why are you taking them?

139
00:12:21,615 --> 00:12:25,427
Is there anything making
you uncomfortable here...

140
00:12:25,427 --> 00:12:26,739
Like what?

141
00:12:26,739 --> 00:12:29,779
I mean, since it's just the two of us here,

142
00:12:29,779 --> 00:12:33,179
you might feel a little uneasy as a woman.

143
00:12:33,179 --> 00:12:34,879
Not really.

144
00:12:36,383 --> 00:12:38,083
That's a relief.

145
00:12:40,391 --> 00:12:42,459
What's your name?

146
00:12:43,339 --> 00:12:46,451
Oh, I'm Kwon Tae Seong, Kwon Tae Seong.

147
00:12:46,451 --> 00:12:50,626
If you're uncomfortable, you can just
give me a fake name or a nickname.

148
00:12:50,626 --> 00:12:53,591
I just need something to call you.

149
00:12:53,591 --> 00:12:56,426
It's Bo Na, Yoo Bo Na.

150
00:12:57,143 --> 00:12:58,995
Oh, Yoo Bo Na?

151
00:12:58,995 --> 00:13:00,695
Yoo...

152
00:13:11,151 --> 00:13:14,471
The pipes aren't going to freeze, are they?

153
00:13:14,471 --> 00:13:16,792
We can just leave the water running a little.

154
00:13:19,323 --> 00:13:23,363
Or the roof collapsing...
from all the snow...

155
00:13:23,363 --> 00:13:25,492
It won't collapse from this much snow.

156
00:13:28,455 --> 00:13:30,259
The gas could get cut off too.

157
00:13:30,259 --> 00:13:31,703
There's a portable stove in the shed.

158
00:13:31,703 --> 00:13:33,403
I see.

159
00:13:34,803 --> 00:13:37,535
What should we make for dinner?

160
00:13:37,535 --> 00:13:41,026
Do you happen to know how to cook?

161
00:14:02,895 --> 00:14:05,327
We should add some soybean paste, right?

162
00:14:05,327 --> 00:14:07,363
I suppose so.

163
00:14:07,363 --> 00:14:09,626
But how much...

164
00:14:10,239 --> 00:14:11,939
Is that too little?

165
00:14:14,659 --> 00:14:16,183
[For stock]
We should add some anchovies, right?

166
00:14:16,183 --> 00:14:17,883
I guess so.

167
00:14:18,819 --> 00:14:19,847
Two?

168
00:14:19,847 --> 00:14:21,139
Two?

169
00:14:21,139 --> 00:14:22,807
- Two?
- Isn't that too many?

170
00:14:22,807 --> 00:14:24,759
At least one each...

171
00:14:26,535 --> 00:14:28,235
Yeah.

172
00:14:39,099 --> 00:14:40,799
What's the problem...

173
00:15:24,643 --> 00:15:26,131
You go ahead.

174
00:15:26,131 --> 00:15:28,126
No, you go ahead first...

175
00:15:50,963 --> 00:15:52,663
Good night.

176
00:16:57,067 --> 00:17:01,279
I'm not usually the type
to get scared easily.

177
00:17:01,279 --> 00:17:03,507
But I've never experienced

178
00:17:03,507 --> 00:17:08,059
a snowstorm this severe,
with such strong winds, in my life.

179
00:17:11,167 --> 00:17:14,471
The power's out, the boiler's down,

180
00:17:14,471 --> 00:17:16,726
there's no phone service,

181
00:17:18,291 --> 00:17:20,703
and we're running out of food...

182
00:17:20,703 --> 00:17:23,392
We're basically refugees, aren't we?

183
00:17:27,799 --> 00:17:30,787
And the snow just keeps coming down.

184
00:17:30,787 --> 00:17:33,059
It'll stop tomorrow.

185
00:17:35,919 --> 00:17:37,759
How do you know that...

186
00:17:49,526 --> 00:17:52,259
Then I'll head back to my room.

187
00:17:52,259 --> 00:17:54,392
Sleep here with me.

188
00:17:56,207 --> 00:17:59,519
You'll freeze to death
sleeping alone in that room.

189
00:17:59,519 --> 00:18:02,292
This is the warmest spot, anyway.

190
00:18:17,019 --> 00:18:19,624
What's the first thing you want to do

191
00:18:19,624 --> 00:18:22,192
when you leave the mountain, Ms. Yoo Bo Na?

192
00:18:24,959 --> 00:18:29,527
I mean, once you go back to your normal life?

193
00:18:29,527 --> 00:18:31,667
Well... nothing, really.

194
00:18:31,667 --> 00:18:33,092
There's nothing you want to do?

195
00:18:33,092 --> 00:18:35,927
Or anyone you want to see?

196
00:18:35,927 --> 00:18:38,192
No, nothing.

197
00:18:39,939 --> 00:18:41,288
Huh?

198
00:18:41,288 --> 00:18:44,092
I came here
because I don't want to do anything.

199
00:18:44,092 --> 00:18:46,026
I just want some peace and quiet.

200
00:19:33,731 --> 00:19:36,795
♪ We wish you a Merry Christmas ♪

201
00:19:36,795 --> 00:19:39,515
♪ We wish you a Merry Christmas ♪

202
00:19:39,515 --> 00:19:42,539
♪ We wish you a Merry Christmas ♪

203
00:19:42,539 --> 00:19:46,126
♪ And a happy New Year ♪

204
00:19:46,855 --> 00:19:49,695
Well, our situation may not be ideal,

205
00:19:49,695 --> 00:19:53,587
but just like you predicted,
the snow has stopped.

206
00:19:53,587 --> 00:19:56,307
And it's Christmas today.

207
00:19:56,307 --> 00:19:58,292
Merry Christmas!

208
00:19:58,943 --> 00:20:00,643
You didn't know, right?

209
00:20:02,367 --> 00:20:08,092
Oh, this is a Christmas present
for you, Bo Na!

210
00:20:32,327 --> 00:20:34,259
Bo Na... Bo Na.

211
00:20:34,879 --> 00:20:39,492
Do you see that little bird
peeking out between the branches?

212
00:20:40,523 --> 00:20:43,092
That wouldn't even be a single bite.

213
00:20:47,899 --> 00:20:51,007
Isn't it tiny and adorable?
So cute and round?

214
00:20:51,007 --> 00:20:54,839
Oh, it's incredible how it survives
so bravely in weather this cold.

215
00:20:54,839 --> 00:20:56,626
Pretty amazing, huh?

216
00:21:15,027 --> 00:21:17,087
Bo Na.

217
00:21:17,087 --> 00:21:19,759
Come over here and look.

218
00:21:21,275 --> 00:21:24,703
What do you think of
when you see icicles, Bo Na?

219
00:21:24,703 --> 00:21:27,826
It'd be perfect for piercing
a vital spot in one go.

220
00:21:33,355 --> 00:21:35,959
Aren't they beautiful and crystal clear?

221
00:21:36,927 --> 00:21:40,319
When I was little, I used to suck on them.

222
00:21:40,319 --> 00:21:42,959
We could make shaved ice with them, right?

223
00:21:52,703 --> 00:21:54,403
Bo Na!

224
00:21:55,847 --> 00:21:57,783
Ta-da!

225
00:21:57,783 --> 00:22:00,187
I found this stuck in the firewood.

226
00:22:00,187 --> 00:22:01,967
Isn't it incredibly romantic?

227
00:22:01,967 --> 00:22:05,392
It was around this time of year
when I first met you.

228
00:22:08,529 --> 00:22:10,759
Can you hold out your hand for a second?

229
00:22:21,411 --> 00:22:23,626
I'll see if I can find another one.

230
00:22:37,103 --> 00:22:39,559
I think the sweet potatoes are almost done.

231
00:22:45,035 --> 00:22:47,026
It's so atmospheric, isn't it?

232
00:22:54,187 --> 00:22:56,826
It would've been nice to have some meat too.

233
00:23:02,259 --> 00:23:05,567
I actually came here to report a story once.

234
00:23:05,567 --> 00:23:07,992
Oh, I'm a reporter.

235
00:23:11,467 --> 00:23:13,167
Anyway,

236
00:23:14,731 --> 00:23:17,507
I parked my car down the mountain
and started walking up.

237
00:23:17,507 --> 00:23:18,682
I must've taken a wrong turn,

238
00:23:18,682 --> 00:23:22,092
and no matter how far I walked,
I couldn't find my way.

239
00:23:22,092 --> 00:23:24,611
I was hungry. My legs were aching.

240
00:23:24,611 --> 00:23:28,371
I thought, "I can't go any farther,"
and just sat down.

241
00:23:28,371 --> 00:23:34,287
But then, I casually turned my head,
and right in front of me,

242
00:23:34,287 --> 00:23:38,059
there was a field of wildflowers.

243
00:23:38,059 --> 00:23:39,351
Like some hidden paradise,

244
00:23:39,351 --> 00:23:44,311
a huge field of flowers spread out
in a place I'd never have expected.

245
00:23:44,311 --> 00:23:47,543
That was the first time
I'd ever felt my heart drop

246
00:23:47,543 --> 00:23:50,335
at the sight of something so beautiful.

247
00:23:50,335 --> 00:23:52,559
As I gazed quietly at the field of flowers,

248
00:23:52,559 --> 00:23:56,059
my heart grew more generous,
and my mood lifted.

249
00:23:57,051 --> 00:24:00,675
Like every cell in my body
was coming back to life, you know?

250
00:24:00,675 --> 00:24:04,811
Thanks to that, I was able to get
my energy back and start moving again.

251
00:24:04,811 --> 00:24:08,092
Oh, and of course, I finished
my reporting without a hitch.

252
00:24:08,883 --> 00:24:11,012
I think that's the power of a beautiful view.

253
00:24:11,012 --> 00:24:13,623
My own little views that give me energy

254
00:24:13,623 --> 00:24:18,435
when I'm tired and help me
get moving again when I stop.

255
00:24:18,435 --> 00:24:21,847
For some people, it could be something

256
00:24:21,847 --> 00:24:27,903
as ordinary as flowers, sunsets,
or stars in the night sky.

257
00:24:27,903 --> 00:24:31,792
For someone else,
it might be a particular moment.

258
00:24:33,671 --> 00:24:36,259
Or even a person.

259
00:24:38,955 --> 00:24:42,726
Have you ever had a beautiful moment
like that in your life, Bo Na?

260
00:24:46,731 --> 00:24:48,871
No.

261
00:24:48,871 --> 00:24:50,692
You haven't? Not even once?

262
00:24:50,692 --> 00:24:54,192
Because I've never thought of
anything as beautiful.

263
00:24:58,126 --> 00:25:00,559
From now on, I'll show you plenty.

264
00:25:05,959 --> 00:25:07,483
I mean...

265
00:25:07,483 --> 00:25:12,759
It's nighttime here
and too dark to see anything pretty.

266
00:25:21,251 --> 00:25:23,659
But there is one beautiful sight.

267
00:25:41,883 --> 00:25:44,426
Oh, the sweet potatoes are going to burn.

268
00:26:05,835 --> 00:26:07,559
Your face is getting burnt.

269
00:26:55,271 --> 00:26:56,971
Why is the gun...

270
00:27:03,047 --> 00:27:04,747
Ms. Yoo Bo Na!

271
00:27:12,427 --> 00:27:14,127
Bo Na!

272
00:27:17,279 --> 00:27:18,979
Bo Na!

273
00:27:26,815 --> 00:27:29,226
Bo Na! Where are you?

274
00:27:42,591 --> 00:27:44,526
Bo Na!

275
00:27:45,595 --> 00:27:47,647
Bo Na!

276
00:27:47,647 --> 00:27:49,559
Bo Na!

277
00:27:52,679 --> 00:27:54,559
Bo Na!

278
00:27:56,427 --> 00:27:58,548
Bo Na!

279
00:27:58,548 --> 00:28:00,426
Bo Na!

280
00:28:07,795 --> 00:28:09,495
Bo Na!

281
00:28:11,164 --> 00:28:12,892
Bo Na!

282
00:28:56,327 --> 00:28:59,059
Why is he lying here like this...

283
00:29:03,267 --> 00:29:05,559
I can't even call an ambulance in this place.

284
00:29:30,626 --> 00:29:34,859
[If I Ever Meet Kingfisher]

285
00:29:36,491 --> 00:29:39,111
As time passed, I became a reporter.

286
00:29:39,111 --> 00:29:40,811
[Spring, 2017]
Mr. Oh!

287
00:29:40,811 --> 00:29:43,659
Do you admit to stock manipulation,
embezzlement, and breach of trust?

288
00:29:43,659 --> 00:29:45,723
There are hundreds of victims!

289
00:29:45,723 --> 00:29:46,959
Don't you feel sorry?

290
00:29:46,959 --> 00:29:52,287
I've watched countless offenders
escape proper punishment.

291
00:29:52,287 --> 00:29:53,455
Mr. Oh!

292
00:29:53,455 --> 00:29:55,626
I've spent countless days feeling despair

293
00:29:55,626 --> 00:29:57,586
as I faced the walls in our society that

294
00:29:57,586 --> 00:29:58,926
no amount of effort
seemed able to break through.

295
00:29:58,926 --> 00:30:00,243
[Kingfisher's Target: A Child Sex Abuser]
The gunman known as Kingfisher

296
00:30:00,243 --> 00:30:01,243
has committed another murder...

297
00:30:01,243 --> 00:30:02,349
But even during that time,

298
00:30:02,349 --> 00:30:04,563
[Kingfisher Victim Exposed For]
Kingfisher continued his work.

299
00:30:04,563 --> 00:30:07,292
[Exploiting Disabled Workers]
Many people tried to figure out who he was

300
00:30:07,292 --> 00:30:09,559
[A Week Later, Kingfisher Strikes Again]
and speculated on why he did such things.

301
00:30:09,559 --> 00:30:10,691
[Victim Was a Gangster]
But I didn't.

302
00:30:10,691 --> 00:30:12,287
Was found shot.

303
00:30:12,287 --> 00:30:15,432
- I never carelessly speculated about him.
- The weight is on the fact

304
00:30:15,432 --> 00:30:17,392
[Rental Scam Real Estate CEO Found Shot Dead]
that it was Kingfisher's crime.

305
00:30:18,771 --> 00:30:21,747
So even if Kingfisher's identity
is revealed someday,

306
00:30:21,747 --> 00:30:23,919
I won't be surprised.

307
00:30:23,919 --> 00:30:26,292
Even if he's someone
who defies all expectations,

308
00:30:26,292 --> 00:30:29,075
like a white-haired old man,

309
00:30:29,075 --> 00:30:33,199
I'll simply look forward to the day
I finally meet him.

310
00:30:33,199 --> 00:30:36,707
I want to sit beside him by the campfire

311
00:30:36,707 --> 00:30:39,743
and listen to him talk about
his life all night.

312
00:30:39,743 --> 00:30:42,771
Like two strangers who met while traveling,

313
00:30:42,771 --> 00:30:46,159
or old friends seeing each other again
after a long time.

314
00:30:47,083 --> 00:30:50,943
Without asking anything,
I could simply listen,

315
00:30:50,943 --> 00:30:55,726
with a warm cup of coffee or tea by my side.

316
00:31:35,939 --> 00:31:37,926
You're awake?

317
00:31:48,983 --> 00:31:51,199
I was so scared.

318
00:31:51,199 --> 00:31:53,359
I was afraid you might disappear.

319
00:31:54,019 --> 00:31:57,126
I'm so relieved, really relieved,
that you came back safe.

320
00:32:05,235 --> 00:32:07,626
Thank you for coming back.

321
00:32:44,235 --> 00:32:46,692
What's this? Where did you get the meat...

322
00:32:47,403 --> 00:32:49,851
I found some in the freezer.

323
00:32:49,851 --> 00:32:53,159
Was there chicken? How did I not see it?

324
00:32:56,987 --> 00:32:58,687
Thank you for the meal.

325
00:33:19,575 --> 00:33:21,727
This is so good.

326
00:33:21,727 --> 00:33:25,392
I think this is the best chicken porridge
I've ever had.

327
00:33:29,651 --> 00:33:32,459
But do you always cry that easily?

328
00:33:36,407 --> 00:33:38,107
Pardon?

329
00:33:41,071 --> 00:33:42,771
No, I don't.

330
00:33:47,559 --> 00:33:50,726
It's actually the first time I've cried
since I graduated from elementary school.

331
00:33:58,827 --> 00:34:00,692
It's a first for me too.

332
00:34:02,359 --> 00:34:04,479
What is?

333
00:34:04,479 --> 00:34:07,292
Someone crying because
they were afraid I'd disappear.

334
00:34:09,175 --> 00:34:11,826
I didn't come here to die.

335
00:34:13,143 --> 00:34:15,859
I've never even thought about wanting to die.

336
00:34:19,911 --> 00:34:22,892
I really... I didn't know you thought that.

337
00:34:23,579 --> 00:34:24,635
Then what about the gun?

338
00:34:24,635 --> 00:34:27,359
I just put it back where it was.

339
00:34:31,219 --> 00:34:33,292
Then what about the gunshot?

340
00:34:34,779 --> 00:34:37,626
It seems like there might be a hunter around.

341
00:34:38,411 --> 00:34:42,495
Right, how did I get here...

342
00:34:42,495 --> 00:34:45,695
Did you carry me here on your back...

343
00:34:45,695 --> 00:34:47,992
I rolled you here.

344
00:34:50,459 --> 00:34:52,159
What?

345
00:34:53,415 --> 00:34:55,826
We're out of water. I'll get you some water.

346
00:35:05,492 --> 00:35:08,159
[Seasoned Salt]

347
00:35:44,403 --> 00:35:46,626
Bo Na, here!

348
00:35:51,267 --> 00:35:54,592
This is the wildflower field
I told you about.

349
00:35:57,243 --> 00:36:01,159
It's my first time seeing the landscape
look like this when it snows too.

350
00:36:04,559 --> 00:36:06,631
I wish there had been flowers here.

351
00:36:06,631 --> 00:36:08,331
But it's winter,

352
00:36:09,427 --> 00:36:11,492
and snow flowers are flowers too.

353
00:36:32,055 --> 00:36:34,292
I like you, Bo Na.

354
00:36:41,743 --> 00:36:44,259
You don't really know much about me, do you?

355
00:36:44,259 --> 00:36:47,159
You're right. I don't know much about you.

356
00:36:47,795 --> 00:36:49,826
I know your name, but...

357
00:36:51,003 --> 00:36:53,026
I don't even know if it's your real name.

358
00:36:53,026 --> 00:36:55,892
I don't know where you were born,
how you grew up,

359
00:36:56,883 --> 00:37:00,579
what your family is like,
or what you do for a living.

360
00:37:00,579 --> 00:37:05,326
I don't know why you were
standing there that day

361
00:37:06,263 --> 00:37:08,099
when we first met.

362
00:37:08,099 --> 00:37:10,726
But I do know some sides of you, Bo Na.

363
00:37:10,726 --> 00:37:12,859
You climb rough mountain paths
without hesitation.

364
00:37:12,859 --> 00:37:15,423
You prefer meat over vegetables.

365
00:37:15,423 --> 00:37:20,067
And in a crisis, you're calmer
and stronger than anyone.

366
00:37:20,067 --> 00:37:21,767
And...

367
00:37:23,523 --> 00:37:27,923
you make the most delicious
chicken porridge in the world.

368
00:37:27,923 --> 00:37:29,919
Perhaps love begins

369
00:37:29,919 --> 00:37:31,999
when you find yourself drawn to

370
00:37:31,999 --> 00:37:35,492
just one side of a person
among all the many sides they have.

371
00:37:37,399 --> 00:37:39,659
I've already fallen in love.

372
00:38:01,247 --> 00:38:04,026
My name is Yoo Bo Na. It's my real name.

373
00:38:05,203 --> 00:38:07,507
Please take care of me.

374
00:38:07,507 --> 00:38:09,559
It's my first time with love.

375
00:38:32,047 --> 00:38:33,792
It's beautiful.

376
00:39:11,192 --> 00:39:15,735
My mom and my older sister
run a chicken shop together.

377
00:39:15,735 --> 00:39:17,815
Do you know what it is called?

378
00:39:17,815 --> 00:39:19,592
Tae Seong Chicken?

379
00:39:22,547 --> 00:39:27,643
My second oldest sister
works at an insurance company.

380
00:39:27,643 --> 00:39:29,543
And the youngest is Se Ah...

381
00:39:29,543 --> 00:39:35,226
So that woman on the rooftop was your sister.

382
00:39:36,403 --> 00:39:38,426
Oh, yes, that's right.

383
00:39:51,195 --> 00:39:54,139
Maybe it's because it's spring,
but you look healthier.

384
00:39:54,139 --> 00:39:56,359
Did you have a good vacation?

385
00:39:57,139 --> 00:39:58,839
Yes.

386
00:40:01,455 --> 00:40:05,159
Have you made up your mind?

387
00:40:14,335 --> 00:40:16,035
My resignation letter...

388
00:40:17,583 --> 00:40:19,631
Please throw it away.

389
00:40:19,631 --> 00:40:21,759
Please forget I ever submitted it.

390
00:40:28,647 --> 00:40:30,347
Alright.

391
00:40:32,391 --> 00:40:34,492
What made you come back?

392
00:40:40,703 --> 00:40:43,059
I saw a beautiful landscape.

393
00:40:43,787 --> 00:40:45,487
What?

394
00:40:50,659 --> 00:40:55,359
The ocean really is the best place
to clear your head, after all.

395
00:41:07,047 --> 00:41:09,295
- Hey, is it good?
- What do you want?

396
00:41:09,295 --> 00:41:11,439
- I asked if it's good.
- Go away.

397
00:41:11,439 --> 00:41:13,292
I said go away!

398
00:41:14,075 --> 00:41:17,135
Go away, hurry, go!

399
00:41:17,135 --> 00:41:19,307
Ma'am, ma'am!

400
00:41:19,307 --> 00:41:20,691
I'll push it for you.

401
00:41:20,691 --> 00:41:22,626
- Huh?
- Who are you?

402
00:41:33,959 --> 00:41:36,426
[Not Today]

403
00:41:36,426 --> 00:41:37,763
[Social Affairs Desk]

404
00:41:37,763 --> 00:41:39,879
Hey.

405
00:41:39,879 --> 00:41:41,939
- Why are you wearing a suit?
- I don't know, man.

406
00:41:41,939 --> 00:41:43,639
You came early?

407
00:41:55,875 --> 00:41:57,271
What's this?

408
00:41:57,271 --> 00:42:02,726
It's to thank you for giving me the chance
to prove myself with my reporting.

409
00:42:04,447 --> 00:42:06,892
Thank you. I'll enjoy it.

410
00:42:07,987 --> 00:42:10,767
I'm about to be completely broke.

411
00:42:10,767 --> 00:42:12,467
Why?

412
00:42:14,875 --> 00:42:15,875
Thank you!

413
00:42:15,875 --> 00:42:17,575
Oh, jeez.

414
00:42:20,239 --> 00:42:21,407
Seriously...

415
00:42:21,407 --> 00:42:25,143
I've also decided to buy
a huge team dinner soon!

416
00:42:25,143 --> 00:42:28,459
A round of applause for our Hae Na!

417
00:42:37,251 --> 00:42:41,411
I made some egg rice this morning,
but I made way too much.

418
00:42:41,411 --> 00:42:43,491
I guess I tend to make too much.

419
00:42:43,491 --> 00:42:45,191
Here.

420
00:42:46,619 --> 00:42:48,503
Are you sure it's safe to eat?

421
00:42:48,503 --> 00:42:50,711
Don't eat it.

422
00:42:50,711 --> 00:42:52,459
I'll just eat it and die.

423
00:43:01,351 --> 00:43:03,659
Sometimes I can't believe it myself, either.

424
00:43:07,235 --> 00:43:10,623
I still can't believe I can cook like this.

425
00:43:10,623 --> 00:43:15,147
Jeez, you should've come to the housewarming.
There was a lot of good food.

426
00:43:15,147 --> 00:43:16,519
I'd just be a burden.

427
00:43:16,519 --> 00:43:18,119
Oh, dear.

428
00:43:18,119 --> 00:43:21,551
Hey, you seriously need to
cut down on instant food.

429
00:43:21,551 --> 00:43:23,355
You'll ruin your health.

430
00:43:23,355 --> 00:43:25,526
Is it good to have a family?

431
00:43:27,339 --> 00:43:28,611
Yeah, it's good.

432
00:43:28,611 --> 00:43:30,492
More than friends?

433
00:43:33,527 --> 00:43:35,359
Friends are...

434
00:43:36,319 --> 00:43:40,492
like guests who sometimes come to the island
where I live, bringing good food?

435
00:43:41,435 --> 00:43:43,159
Family is...

436
00:43:43,887 --> 00:43:47,435
the very island I'm standing on.

437
00:43:47,435 --> 00:43:50,926
My one and only island...

438
00:43:50,926 --> 00:43:53,792
in this endless sea, I guess?

439
00:43:54,726 --> 00:43:56,559
My little piece of land.

440
00:43:58,231 --> 00:44:00,935
You've got something
to protect now, Yoo Bo Na.

441
00:44:00,935 --> 00:44:02,795
You sound just like someone I know.

442
00:44:02,795 --> 00:44:04,495
Huh?

443
00:44:04,495 --> 00:44:06,426
That face of yours.

444
00:44:12,463 --> 00:44:14,003
Do you like it?

445
00:44:14,003 --> 00:44:16,047
It's made from a new lightweight material.

446
00:44:16,047 --> 00:44:18,026
Yeah, I like it.

447
00:44:20,771 --> 00:44:23,259
Can I borrow this for the weekend?

448
00:44:35,647 --> 00:44:38,443
If you're that curious,
why don't you go inside?

449
00:44:38,443 --> 00:44:40,743
What do you mean? I'm not curious.

450
00:44:40,743 --> 00:44:44,235
Those two are friends. They've known
each other since they were kids.

451
00:44:44,235 --> 00:44:48,892
Our brilliant Director Yoo,
and a filthy, smelly shut-in?

452
00:44:52,371 --> 00:44:53,907
What am I, by any chance?

453
00:44:53,907 --> 00:44:56,826
A sickly, obnoxious keyboard jockey.

454
00:44:56,826 --> 00:44:59,492
Jeez, I can't believe this.

455
00:45:04,779 --> 00:45:06,711
You forgot to take this.

456
00:45:06,711 --> 00:45:10,459
Se Ah put a lot of effort into making it.
Wouldn't it be rude not to take it?

457
00:45:16,043 --> 00:45:19,083
Man, a man really needs
to be good-looking, after all.

458
00:45:19,083 --> 00:45:22,431
So this is what they mean by
good looks getting you places.

459
00:45:22,431 --> 00:45:24,619
I know exactly how he feels.

460
00:45:24,619 --> 00:45:27,751
I was exactly like that when I was young.

461
00:45:27,751 --> 00:45:29,492
When?

462
00:45:30,192 --> 00:45:31,483
When I was young.

463
00:45:31,483 --> 00:45:34,492
That girl's got quite a taste...

464
00:45:38,651 --> 00:45:39,728
- It's good.
- Honey, I'll do it.

465
00:45:39,728 --> 00:45:40,863
You didn't even have lunch.

466
00:45:40,863 --> 00:45:42,771
- You need to eat more.
- I'm eating.

467
00:45:42,771 --> 00:45:44,007
- Eat the fish first.
- Okay, I will.

468
00:45:44,007 --> 00:45:45,683
Your favorite fish.

469
00:45:45,683 --> 00:45:47,167
Does your brother not have hands?

470
00:45:47,167 --> 00:45:50,359
The day you return my clothes,
let's go on a date.

471
00:45:59,375 --> 00:46:01,327
You crazy punk...

472
00:46:01,327 --> 00:46:03,726
Why did I even ask her that?

473
00:46:12,315 --> 00:46:14,079
What should I do?

474
00:46:18,891 --> 00:46:20,187
I don't have his number.

475
00:46:20,187 --> 00:46:21,579
Should I ask Bo Na?

476
00:46:21,579 --> 00:46:24,803
Then she'd probably tell me
to bring it to her office.

477
00:46:24,803 --> 00:46:28,826
Then what am I supposed to do about my date?

478
00:46:35,147 --> 00:46:38,359
Yes, Your Majesty. What is the matter?

479
00:46:39,507 --> 00:46:40,731
Jeez, Mom!

480
00:46:40,731 --> 00:46:42,926
I told you not to take orders
from that place.

481
00:46:42,926 --> 00:46:45,726
Why do you keep sending me
all the way over there...

482
00:46:48,143 --> 00:46:51,923
Mom, using highly skilled talent
like me for errands like this

483
00:46:51,923 --> 00:46:55,459
is a waste of national resources!

484
00:47:02,759 --> 00:47:05,926
[Tae Seong Chicken]

485
00:47:16,192 --> 00:47:19,467
[I'm here]

486
00:47:19,467 --> 00:47:21,455
Get off, get off!

487
00:47:21,455 --> 00:47:23,463
Darn it, I'm going!

488
00:47:23,463 --> 00:47:24,791
Let go!

489
00:47:24,791 --> 00:47:26,519
Darn it.

490
00:47:29,135 --> 00:47:30,879
Oh...

491
00:47:34,379 --> 00:47:37,626
The punk came in guilty,
and now he's laughing?

492
00:47:39,715 --> 00:47:42,299
Oh, Se Dol! You got here
sooner than I expected.

493
00:47:42,299 --> 00:47:44,107
Hey, you want to die?

494
00:47:44,107 --> 00:47:46,226
Don't you have a chicken shop
in your neighborhood?

495
00:47:46,226 --> 00:47:47,226
Yeah, we don't.

496
00:47:47,226 --> 00:47:48,944
This neighborhood's nothing but
pizza places and snack bars.

497
00:47:48,944 --> 00:47:51,227
Then eat pizza or snacks around here.

498
00:47:51,227 --> 00:47:53,459
Why are you boosting the sales of
a chicken shop in another neighborhood?

499
00:47:53,459 --> 00:47:55,559
Don't you have any respect
for the local economy?

500
00:47:55,559 --> 00:47:57,326
You brought plenty of
radish and salad, right?

501
00:47:57,326 --> 00:48:01,291
Keep ordering, and you might end up
getting fried with the chicken.

502
00:48:01,291 --> 00:48:02,443
Hey, just wear your helmet properly.

503
00:48:02,443 --> 00:48:04,167
Don't get slapped with a fine for no reason.

504
00:48:04,167 --> 00:48:05,359
I'm going.

505
00:48:05,359 --> 00:48:07,059
Go.

506
00:48:11,823 --> 00:48:13,791
What? I'm busy.

507
00:48:13,791 --> 00:48:17,703
From now on, answer my questions
short and sweet.

508
00:48:17,703 --> 00:48:18,963
Short and sweet about what?

509
00:48:18,963 --> 00:48:21,237
Say you're going on a first date
with some woman.

510
00:48:21,237 --> 00:48:22,523
- What?
- A first date.

511
00:48:22,523 --> 00:48:25,627
- With whom?
- Jeez, I'm just giving you an example.

512
00:48:25,627 --> 00:48:27,387
A hypothetical woman.

513
00:48:27,387 --> 00:48:29,823
- And?
- You ask her,

514
00:48:29,823 --> 00:48:32,259
"What would you like to do?"

515
00:48:33,003 --> 00:48:35,063
What do you mean? We have to eat.

516
00:48:35,063 --> 00:48:37,491
You jump straight to food
the second you meet?

517
00:48:37,491 --> 00:48:39,539
Then what do you do?

518
00:48:39,539 --> 00:48:40,919
Fine. Let's say you have a meal with her.

519
00:48:40,919 --> 00:48:45,283
Then if you say, "Let's get something
to eat first. What would you like?"

520
00:48:45,283 --> 00:48:47,869
What would she say that
you'd find attractive?

521
00:48:47,869 --> 00:48:50,592
Chicken feet! You love those.

522
00:48:51,847 --> 00:48:53,092
I do.

523
00:48:53,092 --> 00:48:57,915
But for a first date,
chicken feet might be a little...

524
00:48:57,915 --> 00:49:01,464
Then your second pick,
all-you-can-eat frozen pork belly?

525
00:49:01,464 --> 00:49:03,191
Jeez, forget the food.

526
00:49:03,191 --> 00:49:04,839
What about the hair?

527
00:49:04,839 --> 00:49:06,539
Bangs down?

528
00:49:08,203 --> 00:49:09,267
Or pushed back?

529
00:49:09,267 --> 00:49:11,583
Definitely bangs down.
You inevitably need to cover up a lot.

530
00:49:11,583 --> 00:49:14,392
Jeez, forget it. Just go eat your chicken.

531
00:49:14,392 --> 00:49:16,126
Jeez.

532
00:49:19,063 --> 00:49:20,992
This isn't about me, you know?

533
00:49:25,335 --> 00:49:27,035
What is she saying?

534
00:49:29,647 --> 00:49:31,347
Hold on.

535
00:49:34,592 --> 00:49:36,163
[If you keep thinking about someone all day,]

536
00:49:36,163 --> 00:49:38,451
[and smile every time they cross your mind,]
Wow, is this for real?

537
00:49:38,451 --> 00:49:41,426
[is that love?]
I'm the only guy around her.

538
00:49:41,426 --> 00:49:42,426
Could it be me?

539
00:49:42,426 --> 00:49:43,556
What do you mean, you?

540
00:49:43,556 --> 00:49:45,271
What? No, it's nothing.

541
00:49:45,271 --> 00:49:46,527
Come into the interrogation room.

542
00:49:46,527 --> 00:49:47,710
Why?

543
00:49:47,710 --> 00:49:48,743
It's about Hwang Cheol Beom.

544
00:49:48,743 --> 00:49:50,443
Now?

545
00:49:52,359 --> 00:49:54,271
Sir, please go ahead and eat this first.

546
00:49:54,271 --> 00:49:56,026
I'm heading to the interrogation room...

547
00:49:56,707 --> 00:49:57,895
Please don't eat my chicken.

548
00:49:57,895 --> 00:49:59,692
- Alright.
- Yeah.

549
00:50:01,226 --> 00:50:03,075
[Tae Seong Chicken]

550
00:50:03,075 --> 00:50:04,759
Ugh, Tae Seong Chicken again!

551
00:50:04,759 --> 00:50:05,859
"Why did you take so long?"

552
00:50:05,859 --> 00:50:07,926
"I reported this ages ago."

553
00:50:09,323 --> 00:50:11,192
"Why aren't you cuffing me already?"

554
00:50:13,355 --> 00:50:16,259
Apparently, he kept saying things like that.

555
00:50:17,355 --> 00:50:18,751
Mr. Hwang Cheol Beom,

556
00:50:18,751 --> 00:50:20,792
why did you do that
right after getting released?

557
00:50:20,792 --> 00:50:22,935
I don't know. Lost my temper?

558
00:50:22,935 --> 00:50:26,447
Oh, so you beat up random people
just because you were angry?

559
00:50:26,447 --> 00:50:30,259
Aggravated assault and bodily injury
will almost certainly get you prison time.

560
00:50:30,259 --> 00:50:34,731
And the sentence will be even harsher
when there are multiple random victims.

561
00:50:34,731 --> 00:50:38,079
Plus, with your prior violent offense,

562
00:50:38,079 --> 00:50:40,392
the repeat-offender enhancement
could keep you locked up for a long time.

563
00:50:40,392 --> 00:50:42,877
You just got out.
You really want to go back in already?

564
00:50:42,877 --> 00:50:44,511
Oh, it's fine.

565
00:50:44,511 --> 00:50:47,492
It's more comfortable in there than out here.

566
00:50:48,264 --> 00:50:51,475
Afraid you'll get shot if you go outside?

567
00:50:51,475 --> 00:50:55,151
You brutally killed your sister-in-law
when she resisted your attempted rape.

568
00:50:55,151 --> 00:50:56,551
You deserved life in prison,

569
00:50:56,551 --> 00:51:00,226
but you fed them that "sudden impulse"
and "mentally weak" nonsense

570
00:51:01,557 --> 00:51:03,759
and got just 15 years.

571
00:51:03,759 --> 00:51:05,563
You're exactly the kind of person
Kingfisher would target, aren't you?

572
00:51:05,563 --> 00:51:09,392
Yeah, I did that because I was afraid of
getting shot and dying. So what?

573
00:51:12,119 --> 00:51:15,523
Do you know what it's like
in prison right now?

574
00:51:15,523 --> 00:51:18,147
Everyone's anxious and making a fuss.

575
00:51:18,147 --> 00:51:20,299
Some guys who've done bad things
but got lighter sentences

576
00:51:20,299 --> 00:51:22,443
are causing trouble inside on purpose

577
00:51:22,443 --> 00:51:25,326
because they're afraid Kingfisher
will kill them once they're released.

578
00:51:25,326 --> 00:51:28,119
Better to stay inside
than to live in anxiety,

579
00:51:28,119 --> 00:51:31,226
shaking at the thought of bullets
flying from who knows where.

580
00:51:31,226 --> 00:51:34,763
Oh, a lot of the guys who got out before me

581
00:51:34,763 --> 00:51:36,672
have gone missing too.

582
00:51:36,672 --> 00:51:39,019
Are you saying some of them were shot dead?

583
00:51:39,019 --> 00:51:40,167
How would I know?

584
00:51:40,167 --> 00:51:42,126
Whether they died from getting shot,
or got hit by a car,

585
00:51:42,126 --> 00:51:44,567
or fell and died...

586
00:51:44,567 --> 00:51:47,564
And for all we know,
Kingfisher doesn't even always

587
00:51:47,564 --> 00:51:50,148
use a gun, right?

588
00:51:50,148 --> 00:51:55,092
Either way, everyone's saying
it's all Kingfisher's doing.

589
00:51:57,319 --> 00:52:02,526
And people can make mistakes in life, right?

590
00:52:02,526 --> 00:52:04,359
Hey, you punk.

591
00:52:05,410 --> 00:52:08,067
What you did wasn't a mistake.

592
00:52:08,067 --> 00:52:10,287
What?

593
00:52:10,287 --> 00:52:14,059
We spent taxpayers' money giving you
a chance to repent and rehabilitate,

594
00:52:14,059 --> 00:52:17,007
and this is what you do
the second you get out?

595
00:52:17,007 --> 00:52:18,383
And what about you people?

596
00:52:18,383 --> 00:52:21,126
Isn't all this happening because the police
can't catch Kingfisher?

597
00:52:21,126 --> 00:52:23,887
Is that why you only targeted
the elderly and women?

598
00:52:23,887 --> 00:52:26,524
Too scared to mess with younger men?

599
00:52:26,524 --> 00:52:29,131
You're just a pathetic coward
who can only prey on the weak!

600
00:52:29,131 --> 00:52:31,392
How dare you run your mouth!

601
00:52:34,091 --> 00:52:37,103
Jeez, he killed innocent people
and calls it a mistake?

602
00:52:37,103 --> 00:52:40,091
You being born is a mistake, you punk!

603
00:52:40,091 --> 00:52:41,976
Hey, Beom.

604
00:52:41,976 --> 00:52:43,718
Pick 20 recently released convicts

605
00:52:43,718 --> 00:52:46,199
who you think got light sentences
for the severity of their crimes,

606
00:52:46,199 --> 00:52:49,571
and find out what's happened to them
since they got out. Hurry.

607
00:52:49,571 --> 00:52:51,587
What? Why?

608
00:52:51,587 --> 00:52:53,051
Oh, you mean guys like him?

609
00:52:53,051 --> 00:52:54,914
Yes, understood.

610
00:52:54,914 --> 00:52:57,515
Did you look into that dead body
at the villa in Hyeonsa-dong?

611
00:52:57,515 --> 00:53:00,539
Oh, the guy who died with his face
in a bowl of jjajangmyeon?

612
00:53:00,539 --> 00:53:02,951
They didn't find anything in the autopsy.

613
00:53:02,951 --> 00:53:05,118
They checked his medical records
for any underlying condition,

614
00:53:05,118 --> 00:53:07,092
but they said there was nothing notable.

615
00:53:08,726 --> 00:53:09,726
Alright.

616
00:53:09,726 --> 00:53:10,869
Finish Hwang Cheol Beom's report

617
00:53:10,869 --> 00:53:12,967
and transfer the case
to the prosecution by tomorrow.

618
00:53:12,967 --> 00:53:14,555
I'm leaving.

619
00:53:14,555 --> 00:53:15,931
Where are you going?

620
00:53:15,931 --> 00:53:17,975
- The supermarket.
- What?

621
00:53:17,975 --> 00:53:19,839
The supermarket?

622
00:53:19,839 --> 00:53:24,226
Oh, boy, now I can finally sleep soundly.

623
00:53:29,492 --> 00:53:32,192
Oh, my legs.

624
00:53:34,539 --> 00:53:36,618
Good grief.

625
00:53:36,618 --> 00:53:42,792
All that scheming just to survive...

626
00:53:43,751 --> 00:53:47,583
But should prison

627
00:53:47,583 --> 00:53:51,395
be a hideout for criminals?

628
00:53:51,395 --> 00:53:56,692
We're already overcrowded as it is,
running out of space,

629
00:53:57,895 --> 00:53:59,747
aren't we?

630
00:53:59,747 --> 00:54:04,259
♪ Dari-dari-da ♪

631
00:54:50,515 --> 00:54:52,215
You're late.

632
00:54:53,463 --> 00:54:55,715
Why am I so bad at this
after not doing it for so long?

633
00:54:55,715 --> 00:54:59,047
How do you remember every year without fail?
Do you have an alarm set?

634
00:54:59,047 --> 00:55:01,059
Open the door. My legs hurt.

635
00:55:01,714 --> 00:55:03,391
Anyone would think you were the son.

636
00:55:03,391 --> 00:55:05,159
Then am I the daughter?
Did you get everything?

637
00:55:05,159 --> 00:55:06,959
I bought it all.

638
00:55:08,326 --> 00:55:11,826
[Lee Pil Ho, Ju Hye Gyeong]

639
00:55:30,192 --> 00:55:33,392
[Lee Pil Ho, Ju Hye Gyeong]

640
00:55:56,475 --> 00:55:58,683
It's almost been 20 years.

641
00:55:58,683 --> 00:56:02,026
Wow. Has it really been that long?

642
00:56:02,843 --> 00:56:05,991
Do you still dream about
what happened that day?

643
00:56:05,991 --> 00:56:09,031
Maybe it's because the ancestral rite
is coming up...

644
00:56:09,031 --> 00:56:10,826
I dreamed about it last night too.

645
00:56:17,011 --> 00:56:18,711
Have a drink.

646
00:56:23,499 --> 00:56:26,531
You talked me into becoming a reporter.

647
00:56:26,531 --> 00:56:28,551
And now that I think about it again,
it pisses me off.

648
00:56:28,551 --> 00:56:30,735
You bring that up every chance you get.

649
00:56:30,735 --> 00:56:32,835
Hey, do you think I wanted to?

650
00:56:32,835 --> 00:56:35,875
You made a huge fuss
about catching the culprit.

651
00:56:35,875 --> 00:56:37,515
And in the end, you couldn't catch him.

652
00:56:37,515 --> 00:56:40,171
Hey, but at least you became a cop, right?

653
00:56:40,171 --> 00:56:42,926
Oh, man, for real.

654
00:56:47,803 --> 00:56:49,811
Are the police in this country
really competent?

655
00:56:49,811 --> 00:56:54,159
If they're that competent, why did it
take them four years to catch him?

656
00:56:58,379 --> 00:57:01,803
That punk still hasn't been released, right?

657
00:57:01,803 --> 00:57:04,526
Not yet. Next year.

658
00:57:06,247 --> 00:57:08,031
Today...

659
00:57:08,031 --> 00:57:11,735
I saw a punk just like him.

660
00:57:11,735 --> 00:57:13,523
That punk said the same thing.

661
00:57:13,523 --> 00:57:16,635
That it wasn't intentional.
That it was a mistake.

662
00:57:16,635 --> 00:57:18,992
I wonder if he's still the same.

663
00:57:18,992 --> 00:57:22,726
No remorse, no rehabilitation.

664
00:57:24,719 --> 00:57:26,959
Has he changed at all?

665
00:57:28,695 --> 00:57:30,399
Pretty. Are these hyacinths?

666
00:57:30,399 --> 00:57:32,859
Yeah, that's right.

667
00:57:34,579 --> 00:57:35,591
Ma'am!

668
00:57:35,591 --> 00:57:38,092
- Yeah.
- I've finished picking out the flowers.

669
00:57:38,092 --> 00:57:39,591
Oh, they're lovely!

670
00:57:39,591 --> 00:57:42,899
Who did our Yul pick such pretty flowers for?

671
00:57:42,899 --> 00:57:45,299
- It's a secret!
- Huh? My goodness.

672
00:57:45,299 --> 00:57:47,159
She's all grown up now,
knowing about secrets.

673
00:57:47,159 --> 00:57:49,015
It feels like just yesterday
she could barely say a word.

674
00:57:49,015 --> 00:57:52,195
Now she often tries to outsmart me.
I can't handle her.

675
00:57:52,195 --> 00:57:53,595
Oh, dear.

676
00:57:53,595 --> 00:57:56,567
Well, even the mighty Yoo Bo Na
has someone she can't beat.

677
00:57:56,567 --> 00:58:00,171
Well, that's what kids are like.

678
00:58:00,171 --> 00:58:02,955
I don't know if I'm doing a good job.

679
00:58:02,955 --> 00:58:04,567
What do you mean?

680
00:58:04,567 --> 00:58:09,392
The fact that you're worrying about that
is proof you're doing a good job.

681
00:58:10,511 --> 00:58:12,483
Now that I think about it, Yoo Bo Na,

682
00:58:12,483 --> 00:58:15,259
it reminds me of when you first had Yul.

683
00:58:16,707 --> 00:58:19,026
And the things you said back then too.

684
00:58:22,095 --> 00:58:23,459
Yul, no! Don't do that!

685
00:58:23,459 --> 00:58:25,371
Oh, dear, Yul, Yul!

686
00:58:25,371 --> 00:58:27,935
No, don't.

687
00:58:27,935 --> 00:58:31,292
Ma'am, what's the room over there?

688
00:58:32,259 --> 00:58:35,126
That's my secret too.

689
00:58:37,927 --> 00:58:39,892
Tell me the truth.

690
00:58:40,635 --> 00:58:42,726
You're a member...

691
00:58:44,215 --> 00:58:46,115
of the Kingfisher fan club, aren't you?

692
00:58:46,115 --> 00:58:48,627
What are you talking about, you crazy punk?

693
00:58:48,627 --> 00:58:54,279
You were obsessed with digging
into Kingfisher until a few years ago.

694
00:58:54,279 --> 00:58:56,111
You were constantly hounding me about it.

695
00:58:56,111 --> 00:58:59,523
Then one day, you just stopped.

696
00:58:59,523 --> 00:59:01,355
Why? Why all of a sudden? Why?

697
00:59:01,355 --> 00:59:03,219
Come on, be honest with me. What? Why?

698
00:59:03,219 --> 00:59:06,343
You're a Kingfisher fan, aren't you?

699
00:59:06,343 --> 00:59:07,906
Hey, enough nonsense.

700
00:59:07,906 --> 00:59:10,603
There's something
I've honestly wondered about for a long time.

701
00:59:10,603 --> 00:59:15,126
Why are you so obsessed with
catching Kingfisher?

702
00:59:16,455 --> 00:59:19,391
You punk, you must be the Kingfisher fan...

703
00:59:19,391 --> 00:59:21,492
Fan club president, right?

704
00:59:21,492 --> 00:59:23,467
- Hey, hey!
- King...

705
00:59:23,467 --> 00:59:27,271
I'm a cop!

706
00:59:27,271 --> 00:59:30,531
Yeah, you're a cop. So what?

707
00:59:30,531 --> 00:59:32,955
You're the family of a crime victim.

708
00:59:32,955 --> 00:59:34,815
I know. I know that too.

709
00:59:34,815 --> 00:59:37,279
Oh, Kingfisher?

710
00:59:37,279 --> 00:59:38,439
He's cool.

711
00:59:38,439 --> 00:59:41,387
Like some hero who takes down evil.

712
00:59:41,387 --> 00:59:45,291
Like a grim reaper taking revenge for me.

713
00:59:45,291 --> 00:59:48,803
But there's a side of him people don't know.

714
00:59:48,803 --> 00:59:52,492
A punk who shot a dad dead

715
00:59:53,851 --> 00:59:57,307
right in front of his seven-year-old son.

716
00:59:57,307 --> 01:00:00,671
Four years ago, at the scene of
Kingfisher's last known crime.

717
01:00:00,671 --> 01:00:05,951
The kid was so traumatized
that he still can't speak.

718
01:00:05,951 --> 01:00:07,659
Jeez.

719
01:00:07,659 --> 01:00:09,019
Hey.

720
01:00:09,019 --> 01:00:14,127
A normal human being
wouldn't kill a parent in front of a child.

721
01:00:14,127 --> 01:00:18,559
No matter how vile the criminal was,
that still isn't right, right?

722
01:00:20,079 --> 01:00:21,329
No matter what anyone says,

723
01:00:21,329 --> 01:00:22,695
- to me, Kingfisher is...
- Yul, is it pretty?

724
01:00:22,695 --> 01:00:24,351
Yeah!

725
01:00:24,351 --> 01:00:30,559
a cold-blooded,
heartless psychopath and murderer.

726
01:00:30,559 --> 01:00:32,726
I feel like I'm going to throw up.

727
01:00:33,719 --> 01:00:36,692
- Huh?
- I seriously feel like throwing up.

728
01:00:39,592 --> 01:00:41,926
Aim properly!

729
01:00:44,039 --> 01:00:46,792
Otherwise, I'll have to clean it up.

730
01:00:47,939 --> 01:00:52,059
If he were just a psychopath
who killed anyone,

731
01:00:52,059 --> 01:00:56,026
it'd be easier to call him pure evil.

732
01:00:57,226 --> 01:01:04,103
But that punk only kills criminals,

733
01:01:04,103 --> 01:01:09,127
so people can't decide
whether he's good or evil.

734
01:01:09,127 --> 01:01:14,415
He taps into the dark side

735
01:01:14,415 --> 01:01:18,591
hidden deep inside everyone.

736
01:01:18,591 --> 01:01:20,826
What a bad punk!

737
01:01:28,211 --> 01:01:30,007
I have something to confess.

738
01:01:30,007 --> 01:01:32,159
You want to die?

739
01:01:33,079 --> 01:01:34,631
Get your hands off me.

740
01:01:34,631 --> 01:01:36,331
I...

741
01:01:38,795 --> 01:01:40,559
I know.

742
01:01:41,359 --> 01:01:44,759
I have a gun at the station, you know?

743
01:01:45,539 --> 01:01:51,719
I... know who Kingfisher is.

744
01:01:51,719 --> 01:01:53,419
What?

745
01:02:09,527 --> 01:02:11,259
Reporter Kwon Tae Seong.

746
01:02:11,867 --> 01:02:16,551
Forget everything that happened today.

747
01:02:16,551 --> 01:02:21,592
And from now on, you'd better
stop looking into Kingfisher.

748
01:02:25,859 --> 01:02:28,292
If you break your promise...

749
01:02:49,779 --> 01:02:51,763
Honey, why are you up so early?

750
01:02:51,763 --> 01:02:53,492
Huh? Well...

751
01:02:53,492 --> 01:02:54,627
Daddy!

752
01:02:54,627 --> 01:02:56,655
Oh, Yul!

753
01:02:56,655 --> 01:02:59,255
Were you playing with Kkongsoon?

754
01:02:59,255 --> 01:03:01,019
Oh, Daddy, you smell like alcohol.

755
01:03:01,019 --> 01:03:02,235
Oh, put me down.

756
01:03:02,235 --> 01:03:03,547
I'm sorry.

757
01:03:03,547 --> 01:03:06,059
I'll brush my teeth and hug you later.

758
01:03:09,819 --> 01:03:12,647
How much did you drink
with Dong Jin last night?

759
01:03:12,647 --> 01:03:14,195
Ugh, I don't know.

760
01:03:14,195 --> 01:03:17,515
He suddenly went on a drinking binge.
What time did I get home last night?

761
01:03:17,515 --> 01:03:18,947
Around 2 AM?

762
01:03:18,947 --> 01:03:22,567
You came home in a taxi, showered,
changed, and went straight to bed.

763
01:03:22,567 --> 01:03:24,215
And you don't remember any of it?

764
01:03:24,215 --> 01:03:25,963
Wow. I must've completely blacked out.

765
01:03:25,963 --> 01:03:27,503
I don't remember any of it.

766
01:03:27,503 --> 01:03:29,067
- Really?
- Yeah.

767
01:03:29,067 --> 01:03:30,191
Really?

768
01:03:30,191 --> 01:03:31,683
Are you going somewhere?

769
01:03:31,683 --> 01:03:34,267
Yeah, I have something
to take care of real quick.

770
01:03:34,267 --> 01:03:36,667
Yul, come eat. Hurry.

771
01:03:36,667 --> 01:03:38,923
It's the weekend.

772
01:03:38,923 --> 01:03:40,663
I'll be back soon.

773
01:03:40,663 --> 01:03:43,479
You can look after Yul while I'm gone, right?

774
01:03:43,479 --> 01:03:44,479
Of course.

775
01:03:44,479 --> 01:03:47,587
I'm still pretty hungover,
but I can handle it.

776
01:03:47,587 --> 01:03:50,311
Honey, you really reek of alcohol.
Go brush your teeth. Hurry.

777
01:03:50,311 --> 01:03:51,831
Sorry.

778
01:03:51,831 --> 01:03:53,935
Yul!

779
01:03:53,935 --> 01:03:55,923
Yul!

780
01:03:55,923 --> 01:03:57,895
That's right.

781
01:03:57,895 --> 01:04:00,092
All right, pick up your spoon.

782
01:04:27,703 --> 01:04:29,419
Hi, Bo Na.

783
01:04:29,419 --> 01:04:31,831
Are your Achilles' heels doing well?

784
01:04:31,831 --> 01:04:33,071
I miss you.

785
01:04:33,071 --> 01:04:34,847
I'll come to you.

786
01:04:34,847 --> 01:04:40,255
I hope I finally get to meet them this time.

787
01:04:40,255 --> 01:04:41,959
From your friend.

788
01:04:45,395 --> 01:04:49,126
I'm sure I talked about
something important...

789
01:04:51,427 --> 01:04:55,926
Daddy, why did you color the rainbow black?

790
01:04:56,539 --> 01:04:59,295
Oh, sorry.

791
01:04:59,295 --> 01:05:01,143
Stop!

792
01:05:01,143 --> 01:05:03,392
I have something to confess.

793
01:05:03,392 --> 01:05:05,759
Actually, I...

794
01:05:05,759 --> 01:05:07,459
I know.

795
01:05:08,651 --> 01:05:10,859
I know...

796
01:05:10,859 --> 01:05:13,326
who Kingfisher is.

797
01:05:34,655 --> 01:05:37,635
Hey, what?

798
01:05:37,635 --> 01:05:40,323
Go home and sleep.

799
01:05:40,323 --> 01:05:42,755
I saw him. I really did.

800
01:05:42,755 --> 01:05:45,019
Saw what? Who?

801
01:05:45,019 --> 01:05:47,799
Kingfisher!

802
01:05:47,799 --> 01:05:49,443
Kingfisher!

803
01:05:49,443 --> 01:05:50,607
Kingfisher?

804
01:05:50,607 --> 01:05:51,795
Yeah!

805
01:05:51,795 --> 01:05:53,592
Really?

806
01:05:53,592 --> 01:05:55,323
Lucky you.

807
01:05:55,323 --> 01:05:58,623
Hey, what does he look like?

808
01:05:58,623 --> 01:06:00,323
Kingfisher?

809
01:06:08,292 --> 01:06:11,426
[Seul Gi]

810
01:06:17,123 --> 01:06:19,219
Kingfisher is...

811
01:06:19,219 --> 01:06:23,839
a tall, well-built

812
01:06:23,839 --> 01:06:25,923
young man.

813
01:06:25,923 --> 01:06:27,623
Who are you?

814
01:06:34,015 --> 01:06:35,799
Oh, Bo Na!

815
01:06:35,799 --> 01:06:37,043
Where are you right now?

816
01:06:37,043 --> 01:06:39,227
Well...

817
01:06:39,227 --> 01:06:41,292
Guess where I am.

818
01:06:41,959 --> 01:06:43,879
Do you know my wife?

819
01:06:43,879 --> 01:06:46,926
What's your relationship with Bo Na...

820
01:06:46,926 --> 01:06:49,923
Nice to meet you, Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

821
01:06:49,923 --> 01:06:53,792
I'm Sergei Volansky, a friend of Yoo Bo Na.

822
01:06:53,792 --> 01:06:55,199
Oh, well...

823
01:06:55,199 --> 01:06:57,459
My Korean name is...

824
01:06:57,459 --> 01:06:59,419
Seul Gi.

825
01:06:59,419 --> 01:07:01,403
I'm Seul Gi.

826
01:07:01,403 --> 01:07:03,759
If you break your promise,

827
01:07:06,303 --> 01:07:10,259
your wife and your child,

828
01:07:10,259 --> 01:07:12,992
your family could be in danger.

829
01:07:51,959 --> 01:07:55,999
You seem to know very little
about Bo Na, Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

830
01:07:55,999 --> 01:07:58,967
I already heard it,
and I can't pretend I haven't.

831
01:07:58,967 --> 01:08:01,051
I have someone I need to protect too.

832
01:08:01,051 --> 01:08:03,692
So those two are your Achilles' heels?

833
01:08:05,115 --> 01:08:06,883
I told you not to show your face
in front of me again, didn't I?

834
01:08:06,883 --> 01:08:09,471
Because you'll end up
betraying me first anyway.

835
01:08:09,471 --> 01:08:12,523
These are the violent offenders
singled out from this year's releases.

836
01:08:12,523 --> 01:08:14,907
Dong Jin, that punk's been released.

837
01:08:14,907 --> 01:08:17,371
He already got a ridiculously light sentence,
and now he's even been paroled...

838
01:08:17,371 --> 01:08:19,519
Do you think he might do something dangerous?

839
01:08:19,519 --> 01:08:22,418
Make it cool, but it won't be easy.

840
01:08:22,418 --> 01:08:24,759
Goodbye, Tae Seong.
